    "author_reviews_count": 11,
    "author_ratings_count": 4,
    "review_text": "We joined Live to Judo shortly after moving to New Zealand three years ago, and it was the very first club our son became part of. I remain incredibly grateful that this was his entry point into sport and structured physical practice.\n\nSimon, the lead sensei, along with Doug, have created an environment that is supportive, inclusive, and appropriately challenging. My child has been part of both the Peewee and Juniors classes, and the instruction has always met him exactly where he was developmentally. The teaching is clearly age-conscious, thoughtful, and grounded in respect for each child as an individual.\n\nSince joining Live to Judo, my son has gained confidence, resilience, and a strong sense of body awareness and autonomy. Just as importantly, he has learned how to challenge himself in a safe, structured way while feeling genuinely supported by his instructors.\n\nWe are very lucky to have a club of this calibre in our local area. Live to Judo has had a meaningful, positive impact on our family, and I would recommend it without hesitation to anyone looking for a judo club that truly understands kids and how they grow.",
