    "author_reviews_count": 2,
    "author_ratings_count": 0,
    "review_text": "When I first walked through the doors of the Live to Judo club, I wasn\u2019t sure what to expect. I\u2019d always been interested in martial arts, but I wanted a place that felt welcoming and disciplined at the same time. From day one, Simon and Doug set that tone perfectly.\n\nThey don\u2019t just teach techniques, they share their love for the art of judo. Simon has a way of breaking down complex movements into simple, clear steps, while Doug brings an energy that makes every session fun and motivating. Together, they create a balance of focus and enjoyment that keeps everyone engaged, from beginners to advanced students.\n\nWhat struck me most is how they build a real sense of community. Every class feels like training with family, people push each other to improve, but there\u2019s always laughter on the mats. Whether you\u2019re working toward competition, self-defence, or just fitness, Simon and Doug genuinely care about your progress.\n\nJoining this club has been one of the best decisions I\u2019ve made. I walk out of every session a little stronger, a little more confident, and already looking forward to the next one. Live to Judo isn\u2019t just a club, it\u2019s a place where you live, live to Judo (North Shore Judo).",
